<p class="kicker">Raise the flag</p>
<h1>Adopt without asking</h1>
<p class="lede">No application, fee or approval. Publish your evidence and say which level you're at.</p>

<h2>Three honest levels</h2>
<div class="table-scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Level</th><th scope="col">What you can claim</th><th scope="col">What it is not</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><strong>Exploring</strong></td><td>You're interested and you've written down your gaps.</td><td>Any conformance claim at all</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Implemented (self-reported)</strong></td><td>You've published evidence links for the pillars you meet.</td><td>Independent certification</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Independently reproduced</strong></td><td>An outside reviewer has reproduced your claim and published their method and results.</td><td>A permanent badge. Claims are tied to a version and a date.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Partial adoption is normal. "4 of 6 pillars evidenced, help wanted on the other two" is a good claim to make.</p>

<h2>Self-assessment checklist</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Code and rights:</strong> a real licence or dedication for your original code, plus a dependency inventory with licences.</li>
  <li><strong>Development:</strong> specs, decisions, agent and tool versions where known, tests, and build instructions a stranger can follow.</li>
  <li><strong>Data:</strong> a working export and import, documented data boundaries, and AT Protocol where it applies, or an honest note on why it doesn't yet.</li>
  <li><strong>Operations:</strong> a deployment and rollback procedure with no secret steps, backup and restore, and a path to another host.</li>
  <li><strong>Economics:</strong> dated, sourced costs. Billed, estimated and donated costs are kept separate, and unknowns are marked unknown.</li>
  <li><strong>Governance:</strong> open proposals, documented decisions, and a succession plan that doesn't run through one person.</li>
</ol>
<p>The full criteria are in <a href="/charter/#conformance">the conformance section</a>. For a machine-readable record, start from <a href="{% sourceLink "templates/open-infrastructure.example.yaml" %}"><code>templates/open-infrastructure.example.yaml</code></a>. It's an illustrative template, not a working integration.</p>

<h2>Tell people</h2>
<p>Raising the flag doesn't need our permission. If you'd like a link from here, open an issue with your evidence. Listing a project here doesn't mean we've audited it.</p>
<p><span class="badge">Adopters listed: 0</span> We won't list adopters who haven't asked to be listed.</p>
